=== Computing Shifted Multiples ===

The problem extends the 'parasitic number' concept:

For digit-shift problem:
  s = d0 * (10^{n+1} - 1) / (10k - 1)
  d0 ∈ {1..9}, k ∈ {2..9}
  Need (10k - 1) to divide d0 * (10^{n+1} - 1)

This is related to the repeating decimal expansion of 1/p:
  If 1/p has period n, then (10^n - 1)/p is cyclic.

For large bounds (up to 10^N), the computation uses:
  - Number theory: modular arithmetic and order finding
  - divisibility criteria for (10^n - 1) / d
  - Generating all valid n up to the bound

PE answer: 119719335
